# shell: desktop
# mount: /devices/board1
# board: only
# A form a board's process publishes, drawn on the desktop.  The board
# ships no interface code: a process declares rows bound to its own
# storage, and the desktop is the program that draws them.  The reads
# below go over the board's console, which has no flow control, so this
# proves what that link delivers reliably: the form opens itself when the
# board is first seen, and shows the board's live values.  Writing a
# control back over a busy console is milestone 5's flow-control work.
wait 25
note the board's form opens itself, titled what the board called it
expect-title Board one
note and shows the board's own values: the name it holds and a reading
note the gauge is bound to
expect-read /devices/board1/gui/demo/name workshop
expect-read /devices/board1/gui/demo/panel gauge Temperature
shot /tmp/trk_boardpanel.png
quit
